  m_Name: Rocky_Thoughts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  loadMode: 1
  saveMode: 1
  saveInterval: 120
  subFolder: Characters/Rocky
  maxEntries: 10
  summary: The miner's struggle with Bayers' formula mirrors Vulkan's curiosity and
    desire for connection. His actions may stem from a need to share his passion
    for technology, potentially using it for good. Laia's photos could be a means
    to inspire change on the island, but their understanding of each other's passions
    may differ.
  entries:
  - I wonder if she's ever thought about how her photos could be used to inspire
    change on this island. Perhaps I can use this opportunity to introduce her to
    my own passion for using technology for good.
  - 'Is this guy a loner or something? He seems to be hiding something. I wonder
    what he wants to achieve by building that camera for Laia... '
  - I'm not sure what's going on with this guy, but I think he might be trying to
    get my attention.
  - Why does Vulkan always have to be so curious? Can't he just leave me alone with
    my thoughts?
  - Still trying to figure out this guy... Formal speech? That's not something you
    see every day...
  - 
  - 
  - I don't know why Vance has to be so condescending. Can't he just listen for once?
    Maybe there's more to Rocky than just his lack of vision.
  - I hope Vulkan understands where I'm coming from, he seems like someone who gets
    me. Maybe he'll see my passion and want to help me in some way.
  - I don't know why, but this guy seems different. He gets me. Maybe there's more
    to life than just proving myself. Could it be that I'm not just carrying on my
    dad's legacy, but finding my own way?
